From 3e78b455ec3b4d141b6c8a5b1dc0ce843df22121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: normy <normy@macbookpro.speedport.ip>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:13:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(collaboration): one teammate-delivery owner for
 every root

RootCommunicationEngine now owns teammate delivery from resolved recipient
to released input for the standalone, AgentOrg and Team roots. Each root
supplies a RootCommunicationPort object; the standalone/Org adapters and
the Team service, adapter and append plan are removed. The engine-owned
one-shot RootMessageAppend runs the open/duplicate/scope checks under each
root's history lock through one coordinator contract, commitMessageAppend.

A Task closing, or the recipient stopping input, after the durable write
is now a normal rejection instead of a root persistence fail-stop
(REQ-012): the record stays, the recipient never gets the input.

Also removes the dead InterAgentMessageRouter and
TaskAgentExecutionRegistry.reserveInput, defines admission validation once
in reserve(), and updates the module docs to the real input path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
